Subject: Screen: a fresh configuration starts fullscreen at the desktop's
 resolution

The default mode (currentScreensetting) is already "desktop resolution,
fullscreen", read from the desktop at run time, so a 720p TV gets 720p and a
1080p one 1080p. But the first fallback when a start fails or is cut short
before the display came up is lastSuccess, which began as a 640x480 window.
On a fresh configuration (no saved mode yet) that window was what the game
then saved as its mode, and it stayed so until the player changed it.

lastSuccess now starts as the same default. Nothing is written to the user's
configuration: only the compiled-in defaults change, and a saved mode (the
ARMAGETRON_* and FULLSCREEN settings) is read over them as before.

diff --git a/src/render/rScreen.cpp b/src/render/rScreen.cpp
--- a/src/render/rScreen.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rScreen.cpp
@@ -85,7 +85,15 @@ static tSettingItem<REAL> at_ca("CUSTOM_SCREEN_ASPECT" , aspect[ArmageTron_Custo
 
 #define MAXEMERGENCY 6
 
+// The last working mode, the first fallback when a start fails or is cut short
+// before the display came up. It starts as the default below (fullscreen at the
+// desktop's resolution), not as a 640x480 window: a fresh configuration whose
+// first attempt fails would otherwise save that window as its mode for good.
+#ifdef DEBUG
 rScreenSettings lastSuccess(ArmageTron_640_480, false);
+#else
+rScreenSettings lastSuccess(sr_DesktopScreensizeSupported() ? ArmageTron_Desktop : ArmageTron_800_600, true);
+#endif
 
 /*
 std::ostream & operator << ( std::ostream & s, rScreenSize const & size )
